const content="<article data-editorial-version=\"3\" class=\"sn-page\"><div class=\"sn-read\"><a href=\"/supporters/\">← Featured sponsors</a><p class=\"sn-kicker\">Marine Diesel Engine · Sponsor feature</p><img class=\"sn-logo\" src=\"/brand/partners/flying-fish.webp\" alt=\"Flying Fish Sailing logo\" width=\"210\" height=\"100\"><h1>Flying Fish: diesel-engine courses and practical sailing training</h1><p class=\"sn-intro\">Flying Fish Sailing offers diesel-engine, maintenance and electrical-system courses alongside sailing tuition in Sydney. For yacht owners, those technical subjects provide a way to learn more about the machinery and systems they use and maintain aboard.</p><img class=\"sn-hero\" src=\"/images/supporters/flying-fish-sailing/photo-1.webp\" alt=\"Flying Fish sailors gathered aboard a training yacht\" width=\"1200\" height=\"1200\"><section><h2>Give engine knowledge dedicated time</h2><p>An owner may spend plenty of time sailing without receiving focused instruction in the engine. Flying Fish includes diesel engines among its wider training subjects, together with yacht maintenance and electrics.</p><p>We like that the school recognises this side of boating. Knowing the vessel involves more than handling the sails, and a technical course gives a subject its own time rather than leaving it to occasional explanations during an outing.</p></section><section><h2>Develop the sailing too</h2><p>Based at Middle Harbour Yacht Club, Flying Fish offers introductory sailing, Day Skipper, Coastal Skipper and Yachtmaster training. Navigation theory and marine radio add other practical subjects, while racing and offshore experiences provide additional time on the water.</p><p>The business has more than 30 years in training and serves recreational and professional goals. Fast-track and modular Yachtmaster programmes give experienced students different pathways to investigate.</p></section><section><h2>Why we feature Flying Fish</h2><p>For readers interested in marine diesel engines, the technical training is the most direct reason to look at the school. It provides instruction in a part of the boat that owners often want to understand better.</p><p>The wider course range means customers can also develop their sailing or work towards a qualification. We appreciate a training business that treats machinery, navigation and boat handling as useful areas of learning within the same boating life.</p></section><div class=\"sn-contact\"><a href=\"https://flyingfishsailing.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"sponsored nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Explore Flying Fish courses ↗</a><a href=\"/supporters/\">More featured sponsors</a></div></div></article><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"Article\", \"headline\": \"Flying Fish: diesel-engine courses and practical sailing training\", \"description\": \"Flying Fish Sailing offers diesel-engine, maintenance and electrical-system courses alongside sailing tuition in Sydney.\", \"image\": \"https://marinedieselengine.com.au/images/supporters/flying-fish-sailing/photo-1.webp\", \"author\": {\"@type\": \"Organization\", \"name\": \"Marine Diesel Engine\"}, \"dateModified\": \"2026-11-05\", \"mainEntityOfPage\": \"https://marinedieselengine.com.au/supporters/flying-fish-sailing/\"}</script>";
